<title>USA: TRADE ESTIMATES FOR USDA WEEKLY GRAIN EXPORT SALES.</title>
<headline>TRADE ESTIMATES FOR USDA WEEKLY GRAIN EXPORT SALES.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade estimates for the U.S. Department of Agriculture's weekly net export sales were as follows (in tonnes). The report is slated for release at 0730 CDT on Thursday.</p>
<p>The old crop marketing year for corn and soybeans ends on August 31, and the old crop marketing year for soyoil and soymeal ends on September 30.</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Estimate Range</p>
<p>Corn (old crop)200,000 to 300,000</p>
<p>Corn (new)     300,000 to 400,000</p>
<p>Wheat	    650,000 to 750,000</p>
<p>Soybeans (old)  50,000 to 125,000</p>
<p>Soybeans (new)-300,000 to+300,000</p>
<p>Soyoil	     3,000 to   6,000</p>
<p>Soymeal  (old)  30,000 to  60,000</p>
<p>Soymeal  (new)  50,000 to 100,000</p>
<p>(Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
